@eavanvalkenburg, can you confirm the direction? Keep `toolConfig.tools` with no `toolChoice` on the final `tool_choice="none"` call, only when the history has `toolUse` or `toolResult` blocks. The fix and a unit test are ready. I'll open the PR once you agree.

One more finding from the live run. When the model still calls a tool on that final request, core drops the call (`_ensure_function_invocation_limit_fallback_response`, `_tools.py:3019`). But `finish_reason` stays `tool_calls`, even though the response has no tool calls left. That happens on both the plain and streaming paths in the table above. The fix would live in the core function loop, not in Bedrock. So I'd keep it out of this PR. Should I file it as a separate issue?

