comment.body:
I'd like to work on this.

Proposed fix: in `_OutputItemTracker.handle`, use the same rule as `Content._add_usage_content` and `AgentResponse.from_updates`:

```python
elif content.type == "usage":
    if content.merge_mode == "replace":
        self._usage_details = deepcopy(content.usage_details)
    else:
        self._usage_details = add_usage_details(self._usage_details, content.usage_details)
```

Why `replace` is safe here: the core function loop (`project_cumulative_usage` in `_tools.py`) already turns per-call `replace` snapshots from Gemini, Bedrock, Mistral and Ollama into running totals for the whole run. So a `replace` that reaches hosting covers every model call so far, not just the last one.

Tests I'd add in `foundry_hosting/tests`: two `replace` snapshots, two `append` updates, and an `append` followed by a `replace`.

One question: the resilient background path starts the tracker from `_HOSTED_PROVIDER_USAGE_KEY`. Its updates come from `Content.from_usage(response.usage_details)` with no merge mode, so they keep adding and this change doesn't affect them. If a `replace` snapshot can ever arrive after a resume, should it replace the persisted usage, or be added on top of it?

@eavanvalkenburg @dargilco could one of you confirm the direction or mark this `ready-for-implementation`? I have the fix and tests ready locally.

